# Course 7 (KEEP; docs/plans/bonanza-courses/KEEP.md): CLOCKWORK KEEP, a floating castle that is one LOCK -
# the first course that is not a line.  A DRAWBRIDGE on a timer, a PORTCULLIS its plate raises, a courtyard
# with the keep's locked DOOR in sight, the ROCKING STAIR (a timed see-saw) up to the battlements, POP-UP
# SPIKES along them to the ring KEY, a drop back to the door, and the COG HALL: two quarter-turn tables over
# a pit, the throne across them.  The cross key, over the TRAITOR'S BRIDGE (down a third of the time), opens
# the TREASURY: exit 1.  Rubber throughout.  PEN-IN, attempt 1: written by
# docs/plans/bonanza-courses/keep/sketch.py --bbc --force while the layout moves.  NOT in the build, NOT
# `guide` yet (KEEP.md's "Risks for refinement").
course KEEP "Clockwork Keep"
width 128
origin 496
ball rubber
uses gate spike seesaw turntable
music fairway             # PLACEHOLDER: the song is the music agent's (KEEP.md: a clockwork march, ticking)
limit 99
target 90

# rooms (the sketch's sections), walls and guard rails
floor rect  22  36  28  40  flat 10   # S: the BARBICAN, 6 x 4
hole  half up tile 22 36          # a diagonal corner
hole  half right tile 27 36          # a diagonal corner
hole  half left tile 22 39          # a diagonal corner
hole  half down tile 27 39          # a diagonal corner
guard rect  22  37  23  39 side -x
guard rect  27  37  28  39 side +x
guard rect  23  39  27  40 side +y
guard rect  23  36  24  37 side -y
guard rect  26  36  27  37 side -y
floor rect  24  32  26  36  flat 10   # D: the DRAWBRIDGE's cells
floor rect  24  29  26  32  flat 10   # G: the GATEHOUSE, 2 x 3
wall  rect  23  29  24  32  flat 11.5   # the gatehouse's cheeks: low, so the courtyard is seen over them
wall  rect  26  29  27  32  flat 11.5
floor rect  20  21  30  29  flat 10   # C: the COURTYARD, 10 x 8
guard rect  20  28  24  29 side +y
guard rect  26  28  30  29 side +y
guard rect  29  25  30  29 side +x
guard rect  29  21  30  23 side +x
wall  rect  29  20  30  21  flat 12.5   # the stair's end wall: the ball waits against it
wall  rect  20  20  25  21  flat 12.5   # the north battlement's inner parapet (and the stair's other end wall)
floor rect  18  18  32  20  flat 12   # B: the north battlement, 14 x 2
floor rect  18  20  20  29  flat 12   # B: the west battlement, 2 x 9
guard rect  18  18  19  26 side -x
guard rect  18  27  19  29 side -x
guard rect  18  18  32  19 side -y
guard rect  31  18  32  20 side +x
guard rect  29  19  32  20 side +y
wall  rect  16  16  18  18  flat 15   # the north-west tower (3 units: a floating face is at most 3, KEEP.md risk C6)
wall  rect  32  16  34  18  flat 15   # the north-east tower
wall  rect  18  29  20  31  flat 14   # the south-west tower (low: it stands in front of the battlement)
wall  rect  20  21  21  23  flat 12.5   # a buttress: a spiked cell may not stand beside a LOWER floor (KEEP.md risk C4)
floor rect  30  24  31  25  flat 10   # the door's sill
wall  rect  30  23  31  24  flat 12   # the door's jamb
floor rect  31  22  34  27  flat 10   # H: the COG HALL's near floor, 3 x 5
floor rect  34  24  36  26  flat 10   # the first cog (a 2 x 2 table)
floor rect  36  24  37  26  flat 10   # the island between the cogs
floor rect  37  24  39  26  flat 10   # the second cog
floor rect  39  22  42  28  flat 10   # T: the THRONE's dais, 3 x 6
guard rect  31  22  34  23 side -y
guard rect  31  26  34  27 side +y
guard rect  39  27  42  28 side +y
guard rect  41  22  42  28 side +x
guard rect  39  22  40  23 side -y
guard rect  41  22  42  23 side -y
floor rect  15  26  18  27  flat 12   # the TRAITOR'S BRIDGE's cells
floor rect  12  25  15  28  flat 12   # the turret, 3 x 3
guard rect  12  25  15  28 side -x -y +y
floor rect  40  21  41  22  flat 10   # the treasury's gate cell
floor rect  39  18  42  21  flat 10   # the TREASURY, 3 x 3
guard rect  39  18  42  21 side -x -y +x
float rect  10  14  44  42
float rect  24  32  26  36 thick 0.5
float rect  16  16  18  18 thick 3
float rect  32  16  34  18 thick 3
float rect  18  29  20  31 thick 2
float rect  15  26  18  27 thick 0.5

prop bridge 24 32 26 36 period 256 on 128 style picket
prop plate 24 30 channel plus
prop gate 24 29 channel plus along y art portcullis
seesaw 25 20 29 21 along x pivot 11 rest + period 128 flat 16
prop popspikes 22 18 period 128 on 64 seed 0
prop popspikes 22 19 period 128 on 64 seed 1
prop popspikes 18 22 period 128 on 64 seed 64
prop popspikes 19 22 period 128 on 64 seed 65
prop key 19 24 channel ring
prop gate 30 24 channel ring along x art door
prop turntable 34 24 size 2 fill oo/..
prop turntable 37 24 size 2 fill oo/.. seed 96
prop bridge 15 26 18 27 period 256 on 96
prop key 13 26 channel cross
prop gate 40 21 channel cross along y

goal  rect 40 24 42 26  flat 10
goal  rect 40 18 41 20  flat 10 exit 1
start 25 38
checkpoint 25 27 ball rubber   # flag 0
checkpoint 24 18 ball rubber   # flag 1
checkpoint 32 24 ball rubber   # flag 2
checkpoint 19 26 ball rubber   # flag 3
checkpoint 14 26 ball rubber   # flag 4

# clocks: on a corner of a floor off the way, or on a tile one out from it
clock 22 38   # start
clock 18 18   # tower
clock 41 27   # throne

# the autopilot's route
way 25 38
way 24 36
way 24 30
way 24 29
way 25 27
way 28 22
way 28 19
way 22 18
way 19 19
way 19 22
way 19 24
way 21 24
way 29 24
way 30 24
way 32 24
way 34 24
way 36 24
way 38 24
way 40 24
# the VAULT way: a branch (the tool's alone)
way 19 24 branch VAULT
way 19 26 branch VAULT
way 18 26 branch VAULT
way 15 26 branch VAULT
way 13 26 branch VAULT
way 15 26 branch VAULT
way 18 26 branch VAULT
way 20 25 branch VAULT
way 29 24 branch VAULT
way 32 24 branch VAULT
way 38 24 branch VAULT
way 40 23 branch VAULT
way 40 21 branch VAULT
way 40 19 branch VAULT
